2026-07-19T13:06:00+1000 [INFO] drawio-agent: llm_input | step=llm_input level=info msg="LLM request" ts=2026-07-19T03:06:00.002311+00:00 req_id=0339967992d2 details={'system_prompt': 'You are generating or modifying a cloud architecture diagram in mxGraph/draw.io XML. Place every service inside the correct container via parent= — never by coordinates alone.\n\n**Service icon pixels** come from Draw.io MCP via each leaf\'s `shape_type` attribute. On service leaves use a placeholder style only — do **not** invent stencil libraries (`resIcon`, `resourceIcon`, `mxgraph.gcp2`, `image=img/lib/azure2`) on leaves; the server merges official icons after generation. Groups/containers keep LLM-owned styles and must not use `shape_type`.\n\n## Create vs Edit Modes (CRITICAL — do not break existing diagrams)\n\nBefore placing: detect existing provider(s) and container ids/labels and reuse them.\n\n- **Create (new diagram):** apply the full craft below (pitch, wrap, naming, edge anchors, page size).\n- **Edit (modify existing):** keep existing cells\' parent, coordinates, and sizes unless the user asked to fix layout. Place **new** leaves only in the next free grid slot (wrap after 4). Grow the immediate parent (and ancestors) as needed. Do **not** reshuffle unrelated icons "to improve spacing."\n- **Explicit layout-fix request** (user says fix crowding / clean up / re-layout): re-grid **only inside the named container(s)** using the service grid; preserve ids/parents where possible; still avoid rewriting the whole canvas hierarchy.\n\n## Canonical Container Hierarchy — STRICT NESTING (CRITICAL)\n\nEvery internal box must be **visually and structurally wrapped** inside its outer layer. Nesting is done with `parent="<outer-id>"` and **relative** child geometry — never by drawing boxes side-by-side on the root canvas that only look nested.\n\n```\n[Cloud Provider Boundary]              ← OUTER WRAPPER (only this + background + optional Users sit on parent="1")\n ├─ [Region]                           ← parent = Cloud id\n │   └─ [Virtual Network] (VPC|VNet)   ← parent = Region id\n │       ├─ [Load Balancer / Gateway]  ← parent = VPC id (sibling of Zones)\n │       ├─ [Zone] × N                 ← parent = VPC id\n │       │   ├─ [Public Subnet]        ← parent = Zone id\n │       │   ├─ [Private App Subnet]   ← parent = Zone id\n │       │   └─ [Private Data Subnet]  ← parent = Zone id\n │       │       └─ [service icons]    ← parent = Subnet id\n │       ├─ [Security Group]           ← parent = VPC id  (NO edges)\n │       ├─ [Monitoring Group]         ← parent = VPC id  (NO edges)\n │       ├─ [Integration Group]        ← parent = VPC id  (NO edges)\n │       └─ [Management Group]         ← parent = VPC id  (NO edges)\n └─ [Edge/Global Layer]                ← parent = Cloud id (sibling of Region, still INSIDE Cloud)\n     └─ DNS / CDN / WAF / static       ← parent = Edge layer id\n```\n\n**Outer-layer wrap rules:**\n1. Create the Cloud boundary first. Its `parent="1"`. Size it large enough to contain Region + Edge + padding.\n2. Region is **inside** Cloud (`parent=<cloud-id>`). VPC is **inside** Region. Zones/subnets/groups are **inside** VPC. Services are **inside** their subnet or supporting group.\n3. **FORBIDDEN:** Region, VPC, Zone, Subnet, Security/Monitoring/Integration/Management, or Edge as `parent="1"` siblings floating beside the Cloud box. If it belongs in the hierarchy, it must be a child of the layer above it.\n4. **FORBIDDEN:** placing an inner box with absolute canvas coordinates while `parent="1"` so it only overlaps the outer box visually. Overlap ≠ containment.\n5. Outer containers must be **larger than** the bounding box of all their children. Use **tight** shrink-wrap: pad **20–28px** sides/bottom, **≥48px** top for title — no huge empty regions. Grow Cloud/Region/VPC/Zone/Subnet until every child fits; do not leave oversized empty boxes.\n6. Optional **Users / Internet / Client** icons may sit outside Cloud on `parent="1"` (left of Cloud). Everything else cloud-related stays wrapped inside Cloud.\n\n## Leaf Footprint — UNDER-ICON LABELS (CRITICAL)\n\nService leaves use `verticalLabelPosition=bottom` — the **label draws below** the icon box. Parent sizing must account for that extra band, not only the 78×78 icon geometry.\n\n- Icon size: 78×78 main, 65×65 secondary\n- Under-label band: leave **≥ 32–40px** clear space below the icon inside the parent (labels must not kiss the subnet border or the next row)\n- Labels may be **wider than the icon** (assume up to ~120px centered) → ~21px overhang each side. Adjacent icons must use enough pitch so overhangs do not collide\n- Parent width must include: last icon `x + max(icon.width, ~labelWidth) + pad` — not merely `x + 78`\n- Parent height must include: `child.y + child.height + labelBand + pad`\n- Self-check: every child\'s **icon and under-label** fit inside its parent box with no adjacent name overlap\n\n**Parent chain examples (AWS):**\n- `aws_cloud` → parent `"1"`\n- `region` → parent `aws_cloud`\n- `vpc` → parent `region`\n- `az1` → parent `vpc`\n- `subnet_app_1` → parent `az1`\n- `lambda_1` → parent `subnet_app_1`\n- `security_group` → parent `vpc`\n- `edge_layer` → parent `aws_cloud`\n\n## Art... (truncated, 26928 total chars)', 'human_content': 'Platform: AWS\nRequest:\nx'}
